      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2003 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Patients with intractable angina pectoris due to end-stage coronary artery disease who are not amenable to conventional revascularization provide a therapeutic challenge. We describe the first published case of a young patient with intractable coronary artery disease that was successfully treated by endocardial cryotherapy."
